,title,link,text,language,family
0,Morori language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morori_language,"Morori is a moribund Papuan language of the Kolopom branch of the Trans–New Guinea family. It is separated from the other Kolopom languages by the intrusive Marind family. All speakers use Papuan Malay or Indonesian as L2, and many know Marind.",Morori,Trans-New Guinea
1,"Bahasa Morori - Wikipedia bahasa Indonesia, ensiklopedia bebas",https://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bahasa_Morori,"Bahasa Morori, atau disebut juga Marori, Moaraeri, Moraori, Morari, adalah bahasa Papua yang hampir mati dari cabang dari keluarga bahasa Kolopom yang merupakan cabang dari Trans–Nugini.",Morori,Trans-New Guinea
2,database of the languages of New Guinea,https://transnewguinea.org/language/morori,"Also Known As: Moraori. Sources: Voorhoeve (1975). Classification: Trans-New Guinea, Moraori.",Morori,Trans-New Guinea
3,Morori | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/mok/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..LddcszyvzbDqP0snH2vNCkzWvhM9VroNFfqOuRwtMY4,Morori is an endangered indigenous language of Indonesia. It belongs to the Trans-New Guinea language family.,Morori,Trans-New Guinea
